  "notes": "GAAP. Governmental lines from governmental funds Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balance (p4, Total Governmental Funds column); business-type from proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses, Changes in Net Position (p6, Total column). Business-type receipts total is computed because the statement prints operating revenues and a nonoperating total net of interest expense; interest expense shown as a disbursement. Balance sheet uses government-wide Statement of Net Position Totals column. Governmental fund transfers out 11,026 = business-type transfers in 11,026 (matches). Detail left empty: the only supplementary schedule (p9, Budget and Actual - All Funds, budgetary basis) combines governmental and utility funds on each line, so it cannot be tagged by fund type, and it is on a different basis from the statements. Roll-forward governmental: 614,142 + 621,226 - 1,061,436 - 11,026 = 162,906 (with itemized receipts 621,225 the difference is 1, see report_discrepancies). Read pages 1-9 of 9 (v8 re-trim: gained p2 Statement of Activities and p8 cash flow reconciliation; both tie to existing figures, nothing new added)"
